# Feature policy

The feature policy provides a single place to identify which Modernisation Platform services an account is opted into or out of.

It allows us to quickly enable or disable services for specific accounts and makes it easier to debug issues or assess which accounts could be affected by a service.

## Where the policy lives

The rules are defined in the [feature policy JSON](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform/blob/main/terraform/feature-policy.json).

To override a feature for a specific environment, add `feature_overrides` to its environment definition. See the [testing-test override example](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform/blob/main/environments/testing.json#L22-L24).

## How it works

Terraform [loads and evaluates the policy](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform/blob/main/terraform/environments/bootstrap/member-bootstrap/locals.tf#L127-L153) using the following priority:

1. Environment feature override
2. Workspace-specific rule
3. Lifecycle and account type rules

The result is available through `local.feature_flags`.

## Supported features

### `instance_scheduler`

Controls whether the Instance Scheduler IAM role and policy are deployed to an account.

The lifecycle and account type rules determine which accounts have this feature enabled.

### `instance_scheduler_testing`

Controls whether the Instance Scheduler IAM role and policy are deployed specifically to the `testing-test` account.

This feature is enabled by the [testing-test workspace rule](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform/blob/main/terraform/feature-policy.json#L54-L60).

## Using a feature flag

Terraform resources use the evaluated feature flag instead of repeating account, lifecycle, or workspace conditions:

```hcl
count = local.feature_flags.instance_scheduler ? 1 : 0
```

See the [Instance Scheduler implementation](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform/blob/main/terraform/environments/bootstrap/member-bootstrap/instance-scheduler.tf#L4).

The [testing-test implementation](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/modernisation-platform/blob/main/terraform/environments/bootstrap/member-bootstrap/instance-scheduler.tf#L57-L70) uses `instance_scheduler_testing` to deploy the required role and policy specifically to that account.

## Overriding a feature

To enable or disable a feature for a specific environment, add `feature_overrides` to its environment definition:

```json
"feature_overrides": {
  "instance_scheduler": false
}
```

Environment overrides take priority over the workspace, lifecycle, and account type rules.